From 1e2f980727acdc4e85e8c96d2b00529e04bebed7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ed <edimoldovan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:09:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] PCI: apple: T6050 adopt: train a port the boot loader
 left down

The adopt path takes a T6050 port only if the boot loader trained its link.
iBoot does not on the J714c: its N1 is held off (SMC GPIO gP13 low, PERST#
low), the shared PCIe PHY is in reset with its clocks off, and Wi-Fi works
only when the port is trained over the m1n1 proxy before the kernel starts.

When the adopt checks find the link down and the port names pwren-gpios,
train it: the shared PHY clocked and out of reset (phy-shared, phy-common),
the RC running, PERST# held and the endpoint powered, then the port enable,
configure and train sequences the root-port reset already uses, and the
bus numbers a boot loader leaves. The adopt checks then run unchanged. The
adopt gate accepts pwren-gpios on such a port.

The root-port configure step now reaches the root port through the ECAM
window: before enumeration there is no pci_dev. The root-port reset uses
the same code.

(cherry picked from commit 0f96cc6c00e1308aa1ba5d9f8e2af5bad61aab0e)
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
